// src/v4/std/nat.dag
//
// Scope: natural numbers — the Peano-inductive non-negative integers; the
//        base of the numeric tower (integer widths and code points build
//        on it).
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_number (Peano axioms)
//
// Owns:
//   - Nat — Peano inductive: Zero | Succ { prev: Nat } (a recursive `Disj`,
//     recursion via Node children per A1 — not a self-referential type)
//   - inhabitance: Nat inhabits `Monoid` (under +) / `Semiring`
//     (std/algebra.dag) — arithmetic falls out of the algebra
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag: Disj
//   - std/algebra.dag: Monoid, Semiring
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-3 (scalar/numeric stack). Replaces
//   part of the deleted std/primitive.dag; see src/v4/STRUCTURE.md
//   §"scalar/numeric concept decomposition".
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).


module v4.std.nat

import v4.std.algebra { Monoid, Semiring, CommutativeMonoid, Semigroup, Magma }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (read before validating against the anchor)
//
// SUBSTRATE — node.dag + algebra.dag only. `Nat` is a recursive `Disj`
// (the `type X = A | B` surface form, recursion through the `Succ`
// payload — exactly algebra.dag's `FreeMonoid` shape; no `Disj` import).
// `Monoid` / `Semiring` and the structures they nest (`CommutativeMonoid`
// / `Semigroup` / `Magma`) are imported from std/algebra.dag to type and
// construct the inhabitance instances.
//
// INHABITANCE IS AN INSTANCE VALUE (operator-ratified). Nat's arithmetic
// grounding is the `data nat_additive_monoid` / `data nat_semiring`
// values below — concrete `Monoid<Nat>` / `Semiring<Nat>`. No `inhabits`
// keyword, no inhabitance carrier.
//
// WHY THE OPERATIONS ARE NAMED FUNCTIONS. `nat_add` / `nat_mul` are
// Peano-recursive, so they cannot be anonymous fn-literals — an anonymous
// literal has no name to call itself by. They are top-level `fn`s the
// algebra instances reference by name (the v3 `timing_lens_monoid.op`
// precedent). This is NOT a parallel public arithmetic API: a consumer
// adds two Nats by walking `nat_additive_monoid` — the named `fn` is the
// algebra instance's content, declared once. (Contrast logic.dag, whose
// finite-domain ops ARE inline fn-literals because they do not recurse.)
//
// TERMINATION. `nat_add` / `nat_mul` each recurse on `prev` — a proper
// sub-Node of the matched argument. That is node.dag A2's IMPLICIT
// structural-descent case: total by construction, no RankingDimension or
// TerminationProof needed (those carriers are for non-structural descent).
//
// LAWS ARE GROUNDED DEFINITIONS, NEVER FLAGS. The monoid / semiring
// axioms (associativity, identity, commutativity of +, distributivity,
// annihilation) are the cited definition of `Monoid` / `Semiring`; the
// recursive equations below are the grounded definitions of + and *.


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Nat — the natural numbers, Peano-inductive: Zero, or the successor of
// another Nat. A recursive `Disj`; recursion lives in the `Succ` payload
// (a Node child per node.dag A1 — regular recursion, decidable).
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_number (Peano 1889).
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1 / modeling-
// discipline.md §4) — classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger —
// five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: Zero / Succ are not per-consumer facts;
//      every structural fold over a Nat handles BOTH (induction base +
//      inductive step). No consumer uses only one.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: the variants have DIFFERENT shapes (Zero
//      nullary; Succ { prev }). Collapsing to `{ is_zero: Bool, prev?:
//      Nat }` makes "Zero carrying a prev" and "Succ with no prev"
//      representable — the inverse of P2 (illegal states unrepresentable).
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: Zero / Succ ARE the Peano constructors —
//      the foundational, intersubjectively-grounded definition of ℕ
//      (Peano 1889). `Monoid` / `Semiring` are imposed ON Nat (the
//      inhabitance instances below), not a richer source Nat derives
//      FROM; nothing in the numeric tower sits below Nat. (Nat is
//      isomorphic to the free monoid on one generator, but that is an
//      equivalent encoding, not a dissolution to something richer — and
//      the scaffold header ratifies the Peano form as the tower's base.)
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a Nat is EITHER Zero OR a successor — genuine
//      mutually-exclusive alternatives (base vs. inductive case), never
//      simultaneous coordinates.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: Zero / Succ are not a mechanical
//      `F<X>` shape repeated over a separately-declared set; they are the
//      two irreducible Peano constructors. No generic / projection
//      (Practice 7) collapses them.
// Terminal: the irreducible Peano inductive definition of the natural
// numbers (Peano 1889) — the root of the numeric tower.
type Nat
  = Zero
  | Succ { prev: Nat }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// nat_add — addition, the Peano recursion on the first argument:
//   0 + b = b ;  (Succ p) + b = Succ (p + b).
// The algebra instance `nat_additive_monoid` references this as its `op`.
// Recurses on `prev` (structural descent — terminating, node.dag A2).
fn nat_add(a: Nat, b: Nat) -> Nat {
  match a {
    Zero => b
    Succ { prev: p } => Succ { prev: nat_add(a: p, b: b) }
  }
}

// nat_mul — multiplication, Peano recursion on the first argument:
//   0 * b = 0 ;  (Succ p) * b = b + (p * b).
// Referenced as the `mul` op of `nat_semiring`. Recurses on `prev`
// (structural descent — terminating); the per-step `nat_add` is itself
// total, so the composition is total.
fn nat_mul(a: Nat, b: Nat) -> Nat {
  match a {
    Zero => Zero
    Succ { prev: p } => nat_add(a: b, b: nat_mul(a: p, b: b))
  }
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// nat_additive_monoid — Nat's inhabitance of `Monoid` under addition. An
// INSTANCE VALUE: the grounding IS this `data`. `op` is `nat_add`;
// `identity` is `Zero` (0 + b = b). Associativity and the two-sided
// identity are `Monoid`'s cited axioms (satisfied by the Peano recursion
// above), never stored flags.
data nat_additive_monoid: Monoid<Nat> = Monoid {
  semigroup: Semigroup {
    magma: Magma {
      op: nat_add
    }
  }
  identity: Zero
}

// nat_semiring — Nat's inhabitance of `Semiring`: the additive
// CommutativeMonoid (Nat addition commutes — the commutativity axiom is
// `CommutativeMonoid`'s grounded definition) and the multiplicative
// Monoid (`op` = `nat_mul`, `identity` = one = `Succ { prev: Zero }`,
// since 1 * b = b). The additive monoid is the SAME authority as
// `nat_additive_monoid` — referenced, not re-built (INVARIANTS P2).
// Distributivity and annihilation (0 * b = 0) are `Semiring`'s cited
// axioms, satisfied by the recursions above.
data nat_semiring: Semiring<Nat> = Semiring {
  add: CommutativeMonoid {
    monoid: nat_additive_monoid
  }
  mul: Monoid {
    semigroup: Semigroup {
      magma: Magma {
        op: nat_mul
      }
    }
    identity: Succ { prev: Zero }
  }
}
